0..75 Comment "// The circle\'s loop space, presented at the term stratum: `Loop(x)` is \"x,"
76..145 Comment "// then the loop\" and `Unloop(x)` \"x, then its inverse\", with the two"
146..220 Comment "// cancellations as rules, so these terms are, one stratum down, the words"
221..295 Comment "// that `Path(Circle, Base, Base)` is in `circle.gandr`, the book\'s circle"
296..370 Comment "// (§ 8.1). Here the mechanism is stated on terms: the presented integers"
371..449 Comment "// model the circle\'s shape with laws that are conversion (`Winding`), a model"
450..524 Comment "// over the native integers owes its laws and a fold into it rests on them"
525..603 Comment "// under `respects` (`NativeWinding`), and the winding number and spinning are"
604..672 Comment "// an equivalence `Words ≃ Int` whose round trips, `sectWords` and"
673..738 Comment "// `retrWords`, are proved by induction over each presented type."
740..766 Comment "// The presented integers."
